cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Kazakh Code-Switching ASR Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark evaluating commercial and open ASR services (fine-tuned and base
  Whisper, Gemini, Google Cloud Speech-to-Text, Yandex SpeechKit) on natural
  Kazakh speech that code-switches with Russian, using a two-layer reference
  (verbatim and normalized) and WER/CER/BERTScore metrics broken down by
  linguistic phenomenon.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Seidalin
    given-names: Timur
license: MIT
keywords:
  - automatic speech recognition
  - ASR benchmark
  - Kazakh
  - code-switching
  - Kazakh-Russian
  - WER
  - CER
date-released: 2026-07-25
